lme2510 — what is not ours

MIT. Copyright (c) 2026 The LME2510 Open Driver Authors. Marker: lme2510-pbcnx.

This repository contains our own code, two vendored third-party components, and facts
observed from vendor material. Read this before redistributing.

1. `vendor/usb/` — pyusb, the Python USB binding.
   License: BSD-3-Clause. Copyright (c) Wander Lairson Costa.
   The full text is in `vendor/usb/LICENSE`. It is vendored so that a checkout runs
   with no `pip install`.

2. libusb — not distributed here. On Windows the driver loads `libusb-1.0.dll`, which you
   install yourself from <https://libusb.info> and point `LME2510_LIBUSB` at. libusb is
   LGPL-2.1, and that license travels with the copy you install. The Java core uses the
   platform's `UsbManager` on Android and does not link libusb.

3. The transport shape in `lme2510/transport.py` and `PacketAligner` follow the
   sibling IT9308 driver (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 The IT9308 Open Driver Authors).
   The Java core uses the same pattern (`Transport`, `Lme2510Device`, `AndroidTransport`).

4. Our own recording of the wire traffic (the lme2510/vendor_trace*.py modules) is our
   work and is shipped: the test suite compares the frames this driver generates against
   it byte for byte. The protocol capture tooling and the raw dumps are not distributed.

5. Facts about the device — USB vendor and product ids, endpoint addresses, register
   and function names, firmware framing — are observations of the vendor application
   and of traffic captured from the device itself. No vendor source code and no vendor
   binary is included in this repository, and none is needed at runtime: every frame
   the driver sends is generated by this package.

6. The vendor firmware images are not distributed here. They are the manufacturer's
   material: supply them yourself, put them in `firmware/`, and the driver checks them
   before use. Broadcast content is not distributed here either.

6. `lme2510` is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
   supported by the manufacturer of the device.
